Modifications by DMD61 (Victory61), 2026:
- Guided sensor dialogs in the HDR wizard and in Verify & report (src/Pages/ProbeGuide.cs, HdrPage.cs, VerifyPage.cs).
- The ArgyllCMS bundled next to the exe is always used first; the bin folder is read-only when it is bundled (src/Core/Argyll.cs, src/Pages/DevicePage.cs).
- Italian translation of the interface (src/i18n/it.json, src/I18n.cs).
- Version 3 (src/Pages/HdrPage.cs, HdrDialogs.cs, ProfilePrompt.cs, ReportExport.cs, SdrPage.cs, MainWindow.xaml.cs,
  Core/ColorProfiles.cs, Charts.cs, App.xaml.cs): opens on HDR or SDR calibration according to the monitor and switches
  Windows HDR on/off by itself; short "Before you start" box with the OSD brightness read over DDC/CI; numbered steps
  in the profile prompt; white-screen warning before step 2; scroll to the next step; name of the final profile;
  closing window (SDR content brightness back to its previous value, test profiles deleted); report export to PDF or
  HTML; chart labels and legends no longer overlap.
- Version 4 (src/Pages/HdrPage.cs, HdrDialogs.cs, ReportExport.cs): HDR colour check (24 colours, ΔE2000) in the final
  verification; report saved automatically at the end (folder and PDF/HTML format chosen with the profile name);
  work folder of the calibration emptied at the end; underscores instead of spaces in the profile name; larger text
  in "Before you start"; reminder for removing colour profiles by hand (colorcpl and the colour folder).
- Version 5 (src/Core/HdrPipeline.cs): the grey curves of the HDR profiles are smoothed and always rising, so the
  probe noise no longer leaves steps in them (banding, coloured where the three channels jumped at different levels).
- Version 6 (src/Pages/PatternsPage.cs, MainWindow.xaml.cs, App.xaml.cs, HdrDialogs.cs, SdrPage.cs, HdrPage.cs, i18n/it.json):
  "Test patterns" page for checking a calibration by eye, also as an independent check (grey ramp, grey steps, shadow
  and highlight detail, colour ramps, saturations, reference colours, full screens); the end of the HDR and SDR
  calibration suggests it (also on the page, with a button that opens Test patterns); the default name of the final HDR profile starts with "HDRDisplayCalibrate"; the white screen of step 2
  (temporary probe profile) is explained in the step card; in Verify & report the LUT switch is marked as SDR only and greyed out
  with Windows HDR on (src/Pages/VerifyPage.cs); step 1 does not start with "SDR content brightness" below 100,
  and it clears the results of the previous calibration so the report holds only the new one.
- Guided sensor dialogs also in SDR calibration and Live meter, and a guide for the room light measurement
  (sensor on the desk, diffuser over the lens) (src/Pages/ProbeGuide.cs, SdrPage.cs, LivePage.cs).
- After the app turns Windows HDR off (SDR calibration, Display & sensor), it restarts the Desktop Window Manager
  through an elevated copy of itself ("--restart-dwm"), because Windows keeps the HDR (MHC2) colour correction loaded
  until then and the SDR colours (and an SDR calibration) would be wrong (src/Pages/HdrOffFix.cs, App.xaml.cs,
  SdrPage.cs, DevicePage.cs); the end of the HDR calibration says to sign out and back in after switching HDR off by
  hand (HdrDialogs.cs, HdrPage.cs).
- Version 7 = 0.3.0-DMD61.7 (everything above since version 6, plus): notice before the SDR calibration turns HDR off;
  the app reopens itself after clearing the HDR correction; version shown in the title bar and in the report
  (src/App.xaml.cs, MainWindow.xaml.cs, Pages/ReportExport.cs, Pages/SdrPage.cs, HDRDisplayCalibrate.csproj).
